  "Question": "Which of the following correctly combines like terms?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(4a^2b-3ba^2=a^2b\\)",
    "B": "\\(3a+2b=5ab\\)",
    "C": "\\(5x^2-2x^2=3\\)",
    "D": "\\(2x+3x^2=5x^3\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(4a^2b\\) and \\(3ba^2\\) are like terms. Their coefficients give \\(4-3=1\\), resulting in \\(a^2b\\). B and D contain unlike terms that cannot be combined; in C, the variable part must be retained after combining, giving \\(3x^2\\).",
